{
  "id": "RLSA-2026:96212",
  "title": "Important: util-linux security update",
  "issued": {
    "date": "2026-11-10 12:01:05"
  },
  "updated": {
    "date": "2026-11-11 00:14:43"
  },
  "severity": "Important",
  "description": "The util-linux packages contain a large variety of low-level system utilities that are necessary for a Linux system to function. Among others, these include the fdisk configuration tool and the login program.\n\nSecurity Fix(es):\n\n* util-linux: util-linux: heap use-after-free in libblkid nested partition probing (CVE-2026-13595)\n\n* util-linux: TOCTOU in the mount program via ancestor directory swap on target path (CVE-2026-53613)\n\n* util-linux: util-linux: Partition metadata compromise via integer overflow in DOS partition parser (CVE-2026-53615)\n\nFor more details about the security issue(s), including the impact, a CVSS score, acknowledgments, and other related information, refer to the CVE page(s) listed in the References section.",
